# The two macOS dylibs under macos-aarch64/ stay ignored, with no exemption.
#
# The loader is 1.4 MB and the KosmicKrisp driver is 15 MB, and git keeps every
# version of a tracked file for ever -- so committing either would charge every
# clone, and every clone of a project using this as a submodule, for binaries
# nobody will run again, including the clones that will never touch macOS.
#
# They are release assets instead, pinned by dylibs.sha256. The driver used to
# be an orphan `driver` branch, which was the wrong shape: a branch stays out of
# a checkout but not out of the object database, and a clone fetches every
# branch whether it wants it or not. `build.sh` and the release workflow fetch
# both with `fetch-dylibs.sh`; `vendor-kosmickrisp.sh` publishes the driver and
# `vendor-vulkan.yml` builds the loader.
/vulkan.c3l
